**RECITALS**

WHEREAS, BioPharma is engaged in the research and development of a novel therapeutic compound, "BP-1234", targeting Chronic Inflammatory Disease (CID);  

WHEREAS, GCR is a clinical research organization with expertise in managing Phase I through Phase IV clinical trials;  

WHEREAS, the FDA regulates the approval of new pharmaceuticals and requires adherence to Good Clinical Practice (GCP) and Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP);  

WHEREAS, both parties desire to collaborate on the development of BP-1234 through a series of preclinical and clinical trials leading to potential FDA approval;  

**NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements herein contained, the parties hereto agree as follows:**

**1. DEFINITIONS**

1.1 "Product" shall refer to the drug compound BP-1234 developed by BioPharma, including any formulations, derivatives, and manufacturing processes associated therewith.  

1.2 "Clinical Trials" shall mean all human testing phases, including Phase I, Phase II, and Phase III, conducted in compliance with FDA regulations and GCP guidelines.  

1.3 "Regulatory Submission" shall mean all documents submitted to the FDA, including Investigational New Drug (IND) applications, New Drug Applications (NDA), and any other required filings.  

**2. SCOPE OF WORK**

2.1 **Development Responsibilities**  
BioPharma shall undertake the following:  
   a. Conduct preclinical studies of BP-1234, including pharmacokinetics and toxicology.  
   b. Prepare and submit the IND application to the FDA by June 30, 2023.  
   c. Collaborate with GCR to initiate Phase I clinical trials by September 1, 2023.  

2.2 **Clinical Trial Management**  
GCR shall be responsible for:  
   a. Designing the clinical trial protocols in accordance with FDA guidelines.  
   b. Coordinating with CTSN to recruit subjects for the trials.  
   c. Collecting and analyzing clinical data, and reporting results to BioPharma and FDA.  

**3. CLINICAL TRIALS**

3.1 **Trial Phases**  
Phase I trials shall commence by September 1, 2023, involving 50 healthy volunteers, with a target completion date of December 15, 2023. Phase II trials shall begin no later than April 1, 2024, enrolling 200 patients diagnosed with CID.  

3.2 **Trial Sites**  
All clinical trials shall be conducted at CTSN sites, specifically at Downtown Medical Institute and City Hospital Research Center.  

3.3 **Reporting Obligations**  
GCR shall provide BioPharma with monthly progress reports, including recruitment status, adverse events, and data analysis. A final report shall be submitted within 30 days of trial completion.  

**4. FDA INTERACTIONS**

4.1 **Regulatory Submissions**  
BioPharma shall prepare all necessary documentation for the FDA, including IND submissions and NDAs, with assistance from GCR.  

4.2 **Meetings**  
BioPharma and GCR shall schedule bi-monthly meetings with FDA representatives to discuss trial progress and regulatory expectations. The first meeting shall occur on October 15, 2023.  

**5. MANUFACTURING**

5.1 **Manufacturing Responsibilities**  
DSMC shall manufacture BP-1234 under GMP, ensuring batch consistency and quality. BioPharma shall provide specifications and quality control measures to DSMC by August 1, 2023.  

5.2 **Batch Production**  
DSMC shall produce the first batch of BP-1234 (1,000 units) for clinical trials by December 1, 2023, and shall ensure all relevant documentation is available for FDA inspection.  

**6. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY**

6.1 **Ownership**  
BioPharma retains all rights, title, and interest in and to the Product and any related intellectual property. GCR and DSMC shall not make any claims to the intellectual property developed during this partnership.  

6.2 **Confidentiality**  
All parties agree to maintain confidentiality regarding trade secrets, proprietary data, and sensitive information exchanged during the duration of this agreement.  

**7. COMPENSATION**

7.1 **Fees & Payment Schedule**  
BioPharma agrees to pay GCR a total fee of $5,000,000, payable in installments:  
   a. $1,000,000 upon execution of this Contract.  
   b. $2,000,000 upon completion of Phase I trials.  
   c. $2,000,000 upon submission of the NDA to the FDA.  

7.2 **Manufacturing Costs**  
BioPharma shall reimburse DSMC for all manufacturing costs incurred, estimated at $500,000 for the initial batch, with an additional 10% contingency for quality assurance testing.  

**8. TERM AND TERMINATION**

8.1 **Term**  
This Excerpt shall commence on March 15, 2023, and shall continue until the completion of all clinical trials and regulatory approvals for the Product.  

8.2 **Termination for Cause**  
Any party may terminate this Excerpt upon written notice if the other party fails to cure a material breach within 30 days of receiving written notice of such breach.  

**9. MISCELLANEOUS**

9.1 **Governing Law**  
This Excerpt shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware.  

9.2 **Dispute Resolution**  
Any disputes arising under this Excerpt shall be resolved through binding arbitration under the rules of the American Arbitration Association.  

